  "label": "Cotton Candy",
  "description": "A sweet, fluffy confection made from sugar spun into threads and often sold on a stick. It is a common treat at fairs, carnivals, and amusement parks, associated with childhood joy and simple pleasures. The meme humorously plays on the idea of the child not having to 'pick it up' (i.e., collect or gather it) but can simply eat it — a common, innocent misunderstanding of how such treats are obtained.",
